Canonical-trigger mint: coverage directives should say up front "questdb: keys include miniquests -- cross the classify:* census (kind field) before reporting quests-covered, and treat steps.jsonl/quests:* research as NOT substrate coverage (the build reads only questdb:/diarydb:)"; without that, a reporter that just counted questdb rows would have published 172/197 -- confidently wrong by 25, in both directions at once (miniquests inflating, researched-elsewhere quests deflating the gap list).
